# Sipeed Tang Primer 20K dock, two pins of it.
#
# PROVENANCE: the dock schematic (Tang_Primer_20K_Dock_3711, sheet
# P007_Things) names ball T3 `Silicone Key_2` and ball N16
# `Orange_LED3`. On the dock, T3 is the button silkscreened S4 and N16 the
# LED silkscreened LED1, which a person established on 2026-09-24 by
# pressing one and watching the other: the silkscreen follows neither the
# net numbers nor Apicula's `examples/primer20k.cst`, which calls N16
# `led[2]`.
#
# The standards are the banks' supplies, from the core board schematic
# (Tang_Primer_20K_Core_board_3690): T3 is in bank 4, the DDR3 bank, on
# +1V5, and the dock pulls the button up to 1.5 V; N16 is in bank 1, on
# VCCO0&1, which is +3V3. A button pulls its pin low when pressed, and an
# LED lights when its pin is driven low.
#
# C13 and A13, the dock's other two LEDs, are the part's DONE and READY
# pins; `reticle fpga` refuses them as IO, because using them so needs a
# dual-purpose setting this flow does not write.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS15 key T3
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led N16
